   "excerpt": "In addition to implementation of their own UDI, EU MDR went one step further with Basic UDI-DI, the key identifier in EUDAMED. Basic UDI-DI is defined as “the primary identifier of a device model. It is the DI assigned at the level of the device family. It is the main key for records in the UDI database and is referenced in relevant certificates and EU declarations of conformity.” [MDR 2017/745, Annex VI, Part C]. So the DI improves the traceability of a family of medical devices over their product lifecycle. [...] There are many interdependencies between other EUDAMED components and the BUDI.",
