   "excerpt": "Medical devices are typically associated with diagnosing, treating, or preventing diseases. However, some products that do not have an intended medical purpose but function similarly to medical devices and pose similar risks are also regulated under the Medical Device Regulation (MDR) (EU 2017/745). These include aesthetic and cosmetic products, such as contact lenses, dermal fillers, and body modification implants. [...] To ensure safety and risk [...] products to comply with many of the same [...] requirements as traditional [...] non-medical [...] fall under MDR [...] . Because of their [..",
