   "excerpt": "One major change introduced by the Regulation (EU) 2017/745 (Medical Device Regulation [MDR]), compared to the former Directives 90/385/EEC (Active Implantable Medical Device Directive [AIMDD]) and 93/42/EEC (Medical Device Directive [MDD]), is the inclusion of products without an intended medical purpose, as listed in Annex XVI of the EU MDR (refer to Table 1 below). This addition was introduced to close a regulatory gap for products without an intended medical purpose but with similar risk profiles to medical devices. These include aesthetic and lifestyle products like colored contact lenses",
