   "excerpt": "The CE mark and the EU Declaration of Conformity (DoC) are two inseparable elements that mark the final and most critical step for a medical device to be legally placed on the European Union market. The CE mark is the visible declaration of compliance, while the DoC is the legal document through which the manufacturer assumes full responsibility. Correctly implementing these requirements is critical, as any errors can lead to delays in market access. [...] The CE mark is not a quality certification issued by the EU, but rather a declaration made by the manufacturer themselves. [...] ##### The ",
